 "Aa rahaa hain soon", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-22T04:03:45Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "The initial public reaction to cameras was very negative. Communities tried to ban them in public places.", "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-22T04:04:00Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "Vats: 10, Akshay: 30, Saumay: 20, Nikhil: 30, Harsh: 5, Prathamesh: 5", "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-22T04:04:04Z", "username": "Harshvardhan Ranade", "text": "Very similar to meta glasses", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-22T04:04:24Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "last question", "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-22T04:04:30Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "10.\tIn the segregated American South of the late 19th and early 20th centuries, a Black sharecropper who walked into the local general store would commonly be made to wait until every white customer present had been served, charged inflated prices for inferior goods, and frequently be refused outright for items the storekeeper considered above his station. The mail-order catalog of X, a Chicago-based company, established in 1892 and reaching its peak of cultural influence in the 1900s and 1910s, was indifferent to the customer's race, accent, or social standing, and it accepted money orders. Recent historical research, notably by economist Marcella Alsan and historian Louis Hyman, has argued that the catalog, commonly called the Wish Book, was one of the most quietly effective tools for Black economic agency of its era. Several Southern White Citizens' Councils organized public burnings of the catalog and pressured local postmasters to “lose” the orders. ID X (10 points).", "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-22T04:04:45Z", "username": "Nikhil Borra", "text": "Macy's?", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-22T04:04:50Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "not Macy's", "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-22T04:04:53Z", "username": "Nikhil Borra", "text": "Bloomingdale's?", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-22T04:04:57Z", "username": "Prathamesh", "text": "Sears?", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-22T04:05:09Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "Answers: X=Sears, Roebuck & Co.", "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-22T04:05:34Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "Sears Tower (now Willis Tower) in Chicago was named for this company", "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-22T04:05:49Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "Final scores: Vats: 10, Akshay: 30, Saumay: 20, Nikhil: 30, Harsh: 5, Prathamesh: 15", "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}]